<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Every user-facing string in the app lives here.

    Rules for anyone adding to this file:
      * Positional arguments only (%1$s, %2$d). Translators reorder them; a bare %s crashes
        the moment a language needs a different word order.
      * Anything carrying a count goes in a plurals element, never an if/else in Kotlin.
        Russian, Arabic and Polish have more than two forms and no amount of branching
        gets them right.
      * translatable="false" for the brand and for unit symbols. "MB/s" and "ms" are written
        the same worldwide; translating them would be wrong, not merely unnecessary.
-->
